            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The acute pain therapy in the setting of conventional or laparoscopic appendectomy has to be initiated by the surgeon. The success of acute pain therapy holds a direct relevance for quality of life, morbidity, chronification of pain, and economic aspects. A written consent between participating occupational groups and medical faculties based on existing guidelines is a crucial prerequisite for a well-functioning acute pain therapy. An adequately informed patient is able to actively take part in the process of his acute pain therapy. He becomes &quot;part of the team&quot;. An efficient acute pain therapy always consists of a combination of non-medical procedures, technical operative aspects, and medical procedures.</AbstractText>
